            <div xml:id="d18">

                <pb facs="0030" n="20" sameAs="frus:frus1941v06/pg20"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00111 A.R./1321: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-06-20T19:00:00-03:00">June 20, 1941—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 10:15 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>695. Referring to telegram to the Department from Montevideo No. 250, June 19, 3
                    p.m., Aranha says that he is sympathetic to the Uruguayan attitude. The
                    Uruguayan Minister for Foreign Affairs <pb facs="0031" n="21" xml:id="pg21"/>
                    has suggested that they meet at Porto Alegre in the near future. Aranha has that
                    under consideration.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Montevideo.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
